    LLM: 'Game: Umtali. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Umtali is a 2-player Rummy game from Rhodesia (now Zimbabwe). 10 cards each. Features 5 meld types: sets (no Jacks), runs, marriages (K+Q same suit for double), single Jacks, and single-card extensions. Opponent gets one final turn after someone goes out. Two-card melds allowed in final turn.',
    objective: 'Players aim to score the most points over four rounds by forming melds (sets, runs, marriages, single Jacks, extensions) and going out; face cards and tens count 5 points each, others 1; marriages score double.',
    gameplay: 'Draw-meld-discard. 5 meld types: Sets (3-4 same rank, no Jacks), Runs (3+ same suit consecutive), Marriages (K+Q same suit = double pts), Single Jacks, Extensions. Deep discard pile draw allowed if meld immediately. Final turn for opponent. Two-card melds OK in final turn.',
